course: dictionary
lesson: 6441
title: Money around the world: the naira
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Every country chooses its own money, called its currency. A currency is the money a country uses to buy things. «Nigeria the naira, the USA the dollar and the UK the pound» shows that each country can have a different name for its money.
explain: The naira is the money of Nigeria. Word problems about Nigeria or shopping there may use naira, so you need to know what it means.
explain: Look for clues in a sentence. If you read «a hundred naira» or «naira notes», you know the money is naira. If a story has prices in naira, the story is probably set in Nigeria.
fact: Naira is the currency of Nigeria.
fact: One naira is divided into 100 kobo.
fact: The sign for the naira is ₦.
fact: Every country chooses its own money, called its currency.
fact: Naira can be a noun for one unit, or used for many: «a hundred naira», «naira notes».
exercise: What is the money of Nigeria called? | Euro | Yen | *Naira | Hryvnia
exercise: One naira is divided into how many kobo? | 1000 kobo | 50 kobo | *100 kobo | 10 kobo
exercise: Which sign shows the naira? | ¥ | ₴ | *₦ | €
test: «Ukraine uses the hryvnia (₴), China the yuan, Japan the yen, Nigeria the naira.» Which country uses the naira? | Ukraine | *Nigeria | China | Japan
test: A story has the line «a hundred naira». What does this tell the reader? | *The story is probably set in Nigeria, where prices are in naira | Everyone in the story is rich | The story is set in Japan | The shop only sells books
exam: What is true about the naira? | It is divided into 10 pence | It is the money of the USA | *It is the money of Nigeria, and one naira is divided into 100 kobo | It is shared by many European countries
